      "text": "The chalky white film that shows up on brick is efflorescence: salts carried to the surface by water moving through the masonry. It's not damage by itself, but it tells you the chimney is wet inside, and on a Fair Lawn chimney that almost always traces back to a cracked top, open mortar joints, or both. Fixing those stops the staining; cleaning it alone doesn't."
