      "text": "On a chimney standing eight feet above the roof, the top courses take the worst of the weather and have the least holding them in place. We see three things on Franklin Lakes' taller stacks: a crack running down from the top through several courses, the top two or three feet leaning slightly off plumb, and a visible gap between the chimney and the house wall where the stack has pulled away. All three usually trace to the same cause — a cracked top letting water into the core for years, freezing and expanding course by course."
