      "text": "A ranch roof pitched at 4/12 or 5/12 doesn't shed water the way a steep colonial roof does. Water moves slowly, snow sits, and leaves and pine needles collect instead of sliding off. On a ranch with the chimney on the main slope, all of that gathers against the uphill side of the brick. Snow banked against the chimney melts from the bottom during the day and refreezes at night, and the water it releases has nowhere to go but under the shingles and behind the flashing."
