      "text": "Stand at the corner of the house and sight up the gap between the chimney and the siding. On a lot of Haworth's exterior-wall chimneys, that gap is wider at the top than at the bottom — the stack is leaning away from the house. Sometimes you can see the gap from across the street; sometimes it's a quarter inch at the eave and the first sign is caulk that keeps splitting, or daylight visible from inside the attic beside the chimney."
