      "text": "The top of a Midland Park chimney was finished with a thin mortar wash around the flue liner, and after 60 to 90 winters it's cracked or gone on nearly every house. Once it's open, rain goes into the top course and down the core, which is what feeds the failing joints and spalling below. It's the first item on most inspection reports and the first repair we'd make."
