      "type": "p",
      "text": "On a solid-brick chimney where spalling has gone through whole faces, a crack runs through several courses, or the stack leans, the section above the roof comes down and goes back up in matched brick, with the flue tiles reset, a poured crown, and new flashing. On a veneer chimney where the brick above the roof has failed, we strip the veneer, repair or reframe the core, install the drainage layer, and re-lay the brick to match the rest of the house — with a stainless pan and crown on top. The section inside the house is left alone in either case."
