      "lead": "The repair",
      "text": "is conservation more than construction. The stack above the roof is taken down to sound brick and rebuilt in reclaimed handmade brick laid in a lime mortar that matches the original — hard Portland mortar on this brick is the one thing we won't do. The top is crowned in a way that doesn't change the chimney's profile from the road, and the flues that are in use are lined with insulated stainless liners sized to each fireplace, which is the only way a 200-year-old unlined flue is safe to burn in. Flues that aren't in use are capped. The attic section is repointed from inside. The fireplaces and the bake oven are left as they are unless the owner wants them worked on — and when they do, firebrick and refractory mortar go in, not modern brick."
