      "text": "A stain on a ceiling or attic framing beside the chimney during rain is a flashing leak. On a center-chimney farmhouse the stack comes through the ridge and the flashing turns the peak corner on a roof that may be standing-seam metal, cedar, or asphalt over several older layers. On the newer homes it's the usual tarred-over flashing and no cricket behind a wide stack."
