      "text": "When spalling has gone through whole faces, a crack runs through several courses, or the stack leans, the section above the roof comes down and goes back up in reclaimed or color-matched soft brick and lime mortar, with any corbel or decorative course rebuilt to the original profile. Flue tiles are reset or replaced, the top gets a poured crown, and the flashing — valley, dormer, and all — is rebuilt in copper. The section inside the house is left alone."
