      "text": "When spalling has gone through whole faces, a crack runs through several courses, or the stack leans, the section above the roof comes down and goes back up — in reclaimed or matched soft brick and lime mortar on the pre-war homes, matched modular red on the postwar ones — and if the chimney was too short, it goes back up taller. Flue tiles are reset or replaced, the top gets a poured crown, and new flashing goes in. The section inside the house is left alone."
