      "text": "When spalling has gone through whole faces — common at the top of a condensing gas chimney — a crack runs through several courses, or the stack leans, the section above the roof comes down and goes back up in reclaimed or matched soft brick and lime mortar, with the flue lined, a poured crown, and new flashing. The section inside the house is left alone."
