      "text": "The signs that a chimney has gone from \"needs work\" to \"needs attention today\": a visible lean that's new or has increased; brick or chunks of mortar on the ground that weren't there last week; a crack running through several courses that you can see daylight through; a top section that moves in wind; or a chimney that's been hit by a limb and is sitting crooked. On a Maplewood lot, any of those over a driveway, a walkway, or a neighbor's roof needs to be dealt with before the next storm."
