      "text": "is the real repair. The old, failed mortar is ground out of the joints to a depth of three-quarters of an inch to an inch, the joints are cleaned, and new mortar — matched to the brick and the original color — is packed in and tooled to the original profile. It restores the joint structurally. It's what a chimney with recessed, sandy, washed-out joints needs, and it lasts 25 to 40 years under a sound crown."
