      "text": "slates around the chimney are removed with a ripper and reset, not cut. Any rotted deck is replaced, the base is wrapped in high-temperature ice-and-water membrane, and step flashing goes in every course, tied into any adjoining valley or dormer flashing. The counter-flashing is set into a reglet ground into the mortar joint — gently on soft brick — or a channel cut into stone, wedged, and sealed. Chimneys wider than 30 inches get a cricket. All of it in 20-ounce copper, soldered."
