      "text": "The signs: a stain in the attic or on a second-floor ceiling under the chimney that has no fireplace below it; a stack that looks lighter and thinner than its twin; a top that's just a cracked slab with no flue tile showing; and on the older ones, a lean or a sag, because the wood frame underneath has been wet for decades. A lot of Westfield owners don't know which of their two chimneys is false until one of them leaks."
