      "text": "The 1950s–70s chimneys have mortar at or past its life — recessed, sandy joints, mortar you can pick out with a key. On the splits, the wall section between the lower and upper roofs is as exposed as the stack and gets skipped by a lot of masons; on the exterior-wall colonials, the full height from grade is exposed; on the lake houses, the lake-facing side takes the wind off the water."
