      "text": "Barns, guest cottages, pool houses, and converted carriage houses on Bedminster's estates have chimneys that fail first and get noticed last — built light, used a few times a year, closed up all winter. Each building's chimney is inspected and written up on its own, and the work is done across the property or building by building."
