      "text": "When spalling or loose veneer has gone through whole faces, a crack runs through several courses, or the stack leans, the section above the roof comes down and goes back up in matched brick — matched as above — with the core repaired, a drainage layer installed, the flue tiles reset or the metal flue re-covered, a poured crown, and new flashing. The section inside the house is left alone."
