  "faq": {
   "heading": "Common questions from Bernardsville homeowners",
   "items": [
    {
     "q": "Our estate chimney is bulging on one side. Does it have to come down?",
     "a": "Usually not. The core behind the face has washed out and the face is standing alone. The core is grouted solid in place, the face is pinned to it, and the chimney is repointed and crowned. A full teardown is for chimneys where the face has already failed."
    },
    {
     "q": "How do you know the core is hollow?",
     "a": "From the top, with a camera and a probe once the cap is off, and from the pattern of mortar loss on the outside. We confirm before we quote the consolidation."
    },
    {
     "q": "Will the repaired stone match?",
     "a": "The stone is the original stone — it stays. The mortar is matched to the original color and sand and finished to the original joint. Replacement stone where a face is relaid is salvaged from the chimney or matched from the same kind of stone."
    },
    {
     "q": "Is the leak from the roof or the chimney?",
     "a": "We inspect from the roof and from the attic before quoting. The attic side shows which chimney the water is coming from and whether it's entering at the flashing or through the masonry, and we put the scope and price in writing."
    }
   ]
  },
